\n\nReason: I choose e2-e4 as it's the most principled first move, immediately fighting for central control, opening lines for piece development, and leading to dynamic positions where White can press for an advantage. This move has stood the test of time as one of the two best opening moves in chess.\n\nAnswer: P: e2-e4"}
