ht-squared bishop\n3. It fights for central control, which is crucial in the opening\n4. It follows fundamental chess principles: control the center early\n5. After d4, White can continue with natural development (Nc3, Bc4/d3, castle)\n6. This move gives White maximum flexibility for future plans\n\n**Answer:** P: d2-d4"}
